# Review package: batch 8, slice keeper

## 0bfa1677 Add the keeper: the app's mode, and the doors from front and the link to the app

The keeper derives maintenance from the updater's status.json and gives the app its word in keeper.json at start and
every second, so an update's state survives a restart of any container. A status file it cannot read changes nothing,
and a word it cannot write costs one log line and closes no door, since the app keeps its mode while the word is stale.

Its two doors carry everything to the app. On the front port x-forwarded-for is believed only from front's address,
looked up by name each time, and no x-forwarded-proto gets through, so the built-in node cannot pass as a visitor or as
the link. The link's http door listens on 127.0.0.1 alone, for the keeper's own frpc, and marks its traffic as https.
While the app is down the keeper answers maintenance during an update and starting otherwise.

config.ts gains machineId from HORNHOOF_MACHINE_ID, and TUNNEL_HOST's message names the keeper container.

Proved by test/keeper.test.ts and test/config.test.ts, written first: the seam with state.ts through freshState, the
app taking link traffic as over the link and front's as local, a forged header from a socket that is not front, the
updater's health check through front in maintenance, and the entry point's ports and its exit. Eight key lines were
broken by hand and each was caught by the test named for it.

Ruling: the plan's acmeDirectory assertion in "loads the keeper's environment and nothing more" is left out - why: this lane's config.ts has no acmeDirectory, it comes with plan 1b Task 7, which has not landed; ACME_DIRECTORY '' is still passed and does not throw - cost if wrong: one assertion to add when 1b T7 lands.
Ruling: maintenanceAnswer takes the JSON or page split from startingAnswer's Content-Type instead of a second copy of the path rule - why: UNDER_API_OR_MCP is private to proxy.ts, which is not this task's file, and one decision lives in one place - cost if wrong: one line, and an export in proxy.ts.
Ruling: the maintenance sentence stands in keeper.ts and in app-mode.ts, and one test holds both answers to the same text - why: app-mode.ts does not export it and is not this task's file - cost if wrong: one exported constant.
Ruling: Keeper.stop() gives connections 5 s and then resolves, whatever is still open - why: the plan does not say, a socket never ends by itself and Docker kills at 10 s, front does the same - cost if wrong: one constant.
Ruling: a keeper.json that cannot be written is logged once until a write works and does not stop the keeper - why: the plan does not say, and its Global Constraints ask to fail toward a working company - cost if wrong: a silent stale word after the one line, which the app already tolerates.

