## e55719a6 Run front, keeper and migrate in place of the tunnel, and start the database for logical copies

Front alone publishes the web port, the keeper holds the peer port and the control folder, and migrate runs once before the app starts. The app drops its port, believes the keeper, and waits for the database, migrate and the keeper. The database starts with the settings logical copies need. The updater keeps no depends_on, since the installer's take-over runs compose up updater without --no-deps. Every port has a :- default so an empty value in a new .env reads as unset. The Dockerfile CMD stays main.js for the app; front, keeper and migrate each override it through command.

The keeper's environment keys are the plan's list: tunnelSettings, readLinkMode and servedCertificate read only databaseUrl, secret, acmeDirectory and machineId, and the keeper reads controlDir, so no field joined the list. RELAY_URL stays as the plan has it.

Ruling: the empty-value test models compose's documented :- rule in a small fill function, since Docker is not run here - why: Docker never runs on this machine - cost if wrong: a compose version that treats an empty value differently would show only at the batch's rehearsal.

